{"homeWinPercentage":0.0639,"playId":"401866466354","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3696","guid":"0e6c7715-3752-3c2d-9ae8-279fdc51b24f","fullName":"Zoeller Field at Dix Stadium","address":{"city":"Kent","state":"OH","zipCode":"44242","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3696.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":8185},"article":{"headline":"Jones' 2TDs help lead Miami (Ohio) to dominant 20-3 win over Kent State","description":"— D'Shawntae Jones ran for 121 yards and two touchdowns, and Miami (Ohio) beat Kent State 20-3 on Tuesday night.","story":"KENT, Ohio -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5193270/d'shawntae-jones\" target=\"_new\">D'Shawntae Jones</a> ran for 121 yards and two touchdowns, and Miami (Ohio) beat Kent State 20-3 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              It was Miami's (7-4, 5-2 Mid-American Conference) fifth win in its last six contests. Kent State (3-8, 2-5) has lost five of its last six.\n\n\r\n              Jones' 1-yard touchdown run on the game-starting drive that went seven plays over 67 yards made it 7-0. A little past the midway point of the first quarter, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5194691/tommy-newcomb\" target=\"_new\">Tommy Newcomb</a> kicked a 39-yard field goal for the Golden Flashes' only points.\n\n\r\n              With 22 seconds before the first ended, Jones again crashed in from the 1 for a 13-3 lead after the missed point-after.\n\n\r\n              Scoring for both teams ended with 9:46 left before the end of the third when quarterback <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5280838/drew-bellisari\" target=\"_new\">Drew Bellisari</a> had a 23-yard scoring run to end a seven-play, 74-yard drive.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/3932733/brandon-jones\" target=\"_new\">Brandon Jones</a> caught four passes for 46 yards for Kent State.\n\n\r\n              The Redhawks outgained Kent State 425 to 170 in total yards. Jones averaged 4.2 yards in 29 carries for Miami.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Miami (OH): Ends the regular season next Tuesday at Western Michigan.\n\n\r\n              Kent State: End its regular season next Tuesday on the road at Eastern Michigan. ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-11-18T15:13:31Z"}}